  <h1>Editorial Standards and Publisher</h1>

  <p>
    wrongfulterminationcalc.com is published by The Click Lab Agency LLC, a California limited liability company based in San Diego. The Click Lab publishes a family of plain-English legal and financial calculators; this site covers wrongful termination and the federal and state laws that govern it.
  </p>

  <h2>Who publishes this site</h2>
  <p>
    Pages are drafted by the publisher&rsquo;s staff, checked against the primary sources listed on the <a href="/methodology/">methodology page</a> (the federal employment statutes, EEOC guidance, and the state statutes named there), and dated with the month of the last review. We do not use invented author names or credentials, and no one who works on this site is an attorney. If you want a named professional to rely on, that is a reason to consult one &mdash; the homepage explains how to reach the EEOC, your state agency, or an employment attorney.
  </p>
  <p>
    Corrections, questions about how a page was produced, and requests to see the sources behind a specific claim can be sent to <a href="mailto:hey@theclicklab.agency">hey@theclicklab.agency</a>.
  </p>

  <h2>Editorial Standards</h2>
  <p>
    WrongfulTerminationCalc follows strict editorial standards to maintain accuracy and independence:
  </p>
  <ul>
    <li>Every legal statement is checked against a primary source before publication, and the page is dated with the month of its last review.</li>
    <li>Statutory information, case citations, and EEOC data are verified against primary sources.</li>
    <li>Content is updated when significant legal developments (new statutes, major court decisions, regulatory changes) affect accuracy.</li>
    <li>We do not accept payment to alter editorial content, and editorial decisions are made independently of advertising relationships. Revenue comes from display advertising, plus a disclosed case-review referral form on the homepage &mdash; see our <a href="/privacy/">privacy policy</a> for details on that separate, optional product.</li>
    <li>We clearly distinguish between factual information and educational estimates. Our calculator results are estimates, not legal advice.</li>
  </ul>

  <p>
    If you believe any content on this site contains an error, please <a href="/contact/">contact us</a>. We take accuracy seriously and correct verified errors promptly.
  </p>

